<!--
  A small Grants.gov daily extract for the end-to-end tests, in the extract's own format.
  {{+N}} / {{-N}} is a date N days from the day the test runs (MMDDYYYY, as Grants.gov writes
  it); tests/e2e/harness.py renders them. Every close date is at least 2 days from a boundary
  the code treats differently (today, 7, 30, 60 and 90 days), so a run that straddles midnight
  or a time zone reads the same. The one fixed date is the placeholder close date, 2076.

  The "profile" keywords are cyber, security and trusted. What each grant is for:
    E2E-TRUSTED      urgent, a 4: comes first in the email though it scores lower than the next
    E2E-NOKW         urgent, a 5, and its description has no profile keyword
    E2E-BULLETS      a 5; the "Institutions of Higher Education" bullet is past character 700
    E2E-ENTITY       a 5; the title is escaped twice, as Grants.gov sometimes sends it
    E2E-PLACEHOLDER  a 5; close date in 2076 and a ceiling of 999,999,999
    DURIP-*          one program posted by three services, same close date
    EXP-2020/2026    a solicitation and its renewal, six years apart
    E2E-BROAD        a broad call, a 2
    E2E-STATES       only state governments may apply: the pre-check scores it 0 itself
    E2E-NOCODES      no EligibleApplicants at all: kept, goes to the model
    E2E-CLOSED       closed five days ago: dropped
    E2E-FORECAST     a forecast: estimated dates
-->
